      "message": "This isn\u0027t doing what you want. `port` is already the active charge port, so this won\u0027t change anything. When we\u0027re running the compliance test, nothing should be plugged into the other port, so what `charge_manager_refresh` will ultimately do is call `board_set_active_charge_port(CHARGE_PORT_NONE)`. But in the general case, there might be something in the other port, so we can\u0027t call that here.\n\nFor the sake of experiment, you should just be able to call `ppc_vbus_sink_enable(port, false);` here. If that works, we\u0027ll need to make a wrapper function that works for boards without PPCs.",
